pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% Regression test (wrong verdict): `RedundanceBasedStrengtheningRule` never overrode
% `Checkable::add_constraints_to_core`, so under `strengthening_to_core on` a `red` written
% without an explicit subproof stored its constraint in the DERIVED set. That set is exactly
% what the mode's shortcut drops: `red` calls `Database::get_proofgoals` with
% `add_derived_goals = false`, which is only sound while everything derived is entailed by the
% core. So the second `red` below never had to preserve `1 y1 >= 1`, and two contradictory
% witnesses refuted a satisfiable formula (x1 alone satisfies it).
f 1;
strengthening_to_core on;
red 1 y1 >= 1 : y1 -> 1 ;
red 1 ~y1 >= 1 : y1 -> 0 ;
rup >= 1;
output NONE;
conclusion UNSAT;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
